765
00:25:58,904 --> 00:26:00,089
- [Mike] Pepé Le Pew over there.

766
00:26:00,089 --> 00:26:02,839
(kissing sounds)

767
00:26:04,390 --> 00:26:06,010
- [Servo] With action hips.

768
00:26:06,010 --> 00:26:07,974
- [Mike] Now is this a
teenager who strangles

769
00:26:07,974 --> 00:26:09,650
or a person who strangles teenagers?

770
00:26:09,650 --> 00:26:11,890
- [Crow] Good question, let's watch on.

771
00:26:11,890 --> 00:26:15,250
- Oh, anytime Vi's a production,
it turns out so well.

772
00:26:15,250 --> 00:26:16,083
- Oh my god.

773
00:26:16,083 --> 00:26:17,460
- Unless it's those jerky
canned onions, and all.

774
00:26:17,460 --> 00:26:18,830
- American Diversified.

775
00:26:18,830 --> 00:26:20,713
It's produced by a food service.

776
00:26:20,713 --> 00:26:22,713
(siren)

777
00:26:25,240 --> 00:26:26,160
- [Servo] Geez look at that.

778
00:26:26,160 --> 00:26:27,590
Even dead she looks great.

779
00:26:27,590 --> 00:26:28,467
She can wear anything.

780
00:26:28,467 --> 00:26:29,633
Oh, I hate her.

781
00:26:33,140 --> 00:26:34,940
- [Crow] I think the dog did it, Ed.

782
00:26:36,293 --> 00:26:37,690
- When did you find the body?

783
00:26:37,690 --> 00:26:40,050
- We got a call about half
an hour ago, Lieutenant.

784
00:26:40,050 --> 00:26:41,477
And then he was there and I investigated.

785
00:26:41,477 --> 00:26:42,310
- I'm a guy.

786
00:26:42,310 --> 00:26:44,087
- Looks like she got
it just like the rest.

787
00:26:44,087 --> 00:26:45,202
- Hm.

788
00:26:45,202 --> 00:26:47,820
- Yes, it's a, it's the same MO.

789
00:26:47,820 --> 00:26:49,470
- [Crow] He means modus operandi.

790
00:26:50,610 --> 00:26:52,100
- Lipstick mark on her forehead.

791
00:26:52,100 --> 00:26:53,020
- Yup.

792
00:26:53,020 --> 00:26:55,170
- [Servo] He's a humorous
killer, isn't he?

793
00:26:56,250 --> 00:26:58,630
- What kind of a nut would
do something like this?

794
00:26:58,630 --> 00:27:00,670
- We're still trying to find that out.

795
00:27:00,670 --> 00:27:03,940
Three weeks ago, it was a
17-year-old girl in Konoba.

796
00:27:03,940 --> 00:27:06,180
Last week a student teacher at the school.

797
00:27:06,180 --> 00:27:07,600
Not much older than this kid.

798
00:27:07,600 --> 00:27:09,570
- [Servo] Let's review the
case in front of everybody.

799
00:27:09,570 --> 00:27:11,106
- Do we take her now, Lieutenant?

800
00:27:11,106 --> 00:27:11,939
(woman laughs)

801
00:27:11,939 --> 00:27:12,800
- It's not funny.

802
00:27:12,800 --> 00:27:14,410
- Okay, Doc.

803
00:27:14,410 --> 00:27:15,573
You can take off now.

804
00:27:16,773 --> 00:27:19,143
- [Mike] Oh, wait, let me
gape at her some more here.

805
00:27:20,670 --> 00:27:21,917
- [Crow] Ready?

806
00:27:21,917 --> 00:27:23,431
(grunting)

807
00:27:23,431 --> 00:27:24,264
- [Servo] Jesus, (indistinct).

808
00:27:24,264 --> 00:27:25,610
Hey, move that keg out
of the way, will you?

809
00:27:25,610 --> 00:27:26,573
That there thanks.

810
00:27:27,650 --> 00:27:29,730
- [Crow] Yeah, yeah, she'll
fit, I'll make her fit.

811
00:27:29,730 --> 00:27:31,170
There, always room.

812
00:27:31,170 --> 00:27:32,003
See.

813
00:27:34,700 --> 00:27:37,150
- [Mike] Well those
ambulance guy seem real nice.

814
00:27:38,430 --> 00:27:40,233
- [Servo] Pump it, there we go.

815
00:27:41,083 --> 00:27:42,600
(siren)

816
00:27:42,600 --> 00:27:44,450
- [Mike] Yeah, there was
talk about having lunch,

817
00:27:44,450 --> 00:27:46,047
but just never get to it.

818
00:27:46,047 --> 00:27:47,973
[Crow] I need a Snicker bar.

819
00:27:50,032 --> 00:27:51,657
- [Mike] (indistinct), please.

820
00:27:51,657 --> 00:27:52,857
- Lieutenant Anderson to headquarters.

821
00:27:52,857 --> 00:27:53,887
- [Servo] Anderson, that's me.

822
00:27:53,887 --> 00:27:55,100
- [Man] Headquarters,
go ahead, Lieutenant.

823
00:27:55,100 --> 00:27:56,760
- We've finished here, they've
taken the body to the morgue.

824
00:27:56,760 --> 00:27:58,236
- [Mike] That guy's in the back seat.

825
00:27:58,236 --> 00:27:59,069
- [Man] (indistinct) wants to know

826
00:27:59,069 --> 00:28:01,190
if you've got any new clues?

827
00:28:01,190 --> 00:28:02,707
- No, nothing more than before.

828
00:28:02,707 --> 00:28:03,540
- [Crow] And don't rush me.

829
00:28:03,540 --> 00:28:05,510
- It's the same one.

830
00:28:05,510 --> 00:28:06,750
Tell Captain Murdoch, I'll be in

831
00:28:06,750 --> 00:28:08,500
as soon as I've finished around here.

832
00:28:08,500 --> 00:28:10,930
Oh, and you better have
a couple of the boys

833
00:28:10,930 --> 00:28:12,520
down here to help Bill.

834
00:28:12,520 --> 00:28:13,648
Are you 10-4?

835
00:28:13,648 --> 00:28:15,231
- [Man] 10-4.

836
00:28:15,231 --> 00:28:16,064
- Okay.

837
00:28:16,064 --> 00:28:17,253
- [Crow] 10-4, that's
official cop talk, you know?

838
00:28:18,826 --> 00:28:19,659
- Now, you'll have some help.

839
00:28:19,659 --> 00:28:22,700
I want you to comb this whole
area, check out everything,

840
00:28:22,700 --> 00:28:25,105
street houses, everything in sight.

841
00:28:25,105 --> 00:28:25,938
- [Servo] But, Captain I-

842
00:28:25,938 --> 00:28:27,050
- I've got some things
to attend at morgue.

843
00:28:27,050 --> 00:28:29,350
- [Servo] But I'm the milk man.

844
00:28:29,350 --> 00:28:31,494
Guess I'll could leave him some yogurt.

845
00:28:31,494 --> 00:28:32,560
- [Mike] Well, I'll get through tomorrow,

846
00:28:32,560 --> 00:28:35,497
what could possible happen
between now and then?

847
00:28:35,497 --> 00:28:37,352
(siren)

848
00:28:37,352 --> 00:28:38,935
- [Crow] Who cares.

849
00:28:42,610 --> 00:28:45,010
- [Servo] Six-ten, I
return to the Best Western.

850
00:28:46,240 --> 00:28:47,640
- [Crow] Mamie Eisenhower.

851
00:28:47,640 --> 00:28:49,109
- No, (indistinct) we
don't know who it was.

852
00:28:49,109 --> 00:28:50,192
- [Servo] What was that?

853
00:28:50,192 --> 00:28:51,066
- [Mike] I don't.

854
00:28:51,066 --> 00:28:52,410
- But it made nos sense
until this morning.

855
00:28:52,410 --> 00:28:53,595
- [Mike] Yes, I explain golf.

856
00:28:53,595 --> 00:28:55,130
- Yes, we called the police.

857
00:28:55,130 --> 00:28:56,660
- [Servo] Yes, he's dead, dead, dead.

858
00:28:56,660 --> 00:28:59,470
- As a matter of fact, we're
expecting them at any moment.

859
00:28:59,470 --> 00:29:01,800
- [Crow] Six-eleven, they were
expecting us at any moment.

860
00:29:01,800 --> 00:29:02,633
I ring the bell.

861
00:29:04,023 --> 00:29:06,710
- The door bell's ringing,
that must be them now.

862
00:29:06,710 --> 00:29:07,963
I've got to hang up.

863
00:29:09,530 --> 00:29:10,526
Yes.

864
00:29:10,526 --> 00:29:11,620
- [Servo] Okay, I'll join the ACLU.

865
00:29:11,620 --> 00:29:12,870
- Yes, yes, I'll call your right back.

866
00:29:12,870 --> 00:29:15,411
- [Mike] From community
theater to the be big screen.

867
00:29:15,411 --> 00:29:17,570
- [Crow] Now remember the three S's.

868
00:29:17,570 --> 00:29:19,123
Smile, star, strong.

869
00:29:21,680 --> 00:29:22,513
- Oh.

870
00:29:22,513 --> 00:29:23,787
- I'm Lieutenant Anderson.

871
00:29:23,787 --> 00:29:24,620
Homicide division.

872
00:29:24,620 --> 00:29:25,610
- [Servo] Drop the poodle and step away

873
00:29:25,610 --> 00:29:26,823
from the condo please.

874
00:29:27,660 --> 00:29:28,881
- Only one of you?

875
00:29:28,881 --> 00:29:29,714
- [Mike] (indistinct) Wilson.

876
00:29:29,714 --> 00:29:31,410
- I'm Betty's mother, Mrs. Royson.

877
00:29:31,410 --> 00:29:33,040
We've been expecting you.

878
00:29:33,040 --> 00:29:34,735
They'd phoned you'd come.

879
00:29:34,735 --> 00:29:36,280
Let's go into the living room.

880
00:29:36,280 --> 00:29:37,375
My husband's in there.

881
00:29:37,375 --> 00:29:38,208
(robot laughs)

882
00:29:38,208 --> 00:29:39,041
- [Crow] You're quite handsome.

883
00:29:39,041 --> 00:29:39,874
Can I touch your gun?

884
00:29:41,614 --> 00:29:42,600
(door closes)

885
00:29:42,600 --> 00:29:44,330
- [Mike] Do we start
with stern questioning?

886
00:29:44,330 --> 00:29:46,250
When do you become physical with me?

887
00:29:46,250 --> 00:29:47,970
- Dear, this is Lieutenant Anderson.

888
00:29:47,970 --> 00:29:49,480
- [Servo] Anderson, that's me.

889
00:29:51,146 --> 00:29:52,263
- How do you do, Lieutenant?

890
00:29:52,263 --> 00:29:54,750
Now, I knew a policemen
once back in my home town.

891
00:29:54,750 --> 00:29:55,583
- [Crow] Didn't like him.

892
00:29:55,583 --> 00:29:57,120
- His name was Hertison.

893
00:29:57,120 --> 00:29:59,000
- The name I have is Anderson.

894
00:29:59,000 --> 00:29:59,833
- [Servo] That's me.

895
00:29:59,833 --> 00:30:02,380
- Mr. Royson, I'm here on police business.

896
00:30:02,380 --> 00:30:04,197
- Sit down, would you?

897
00:30:04,197 --> 00:30:05,433
(farting effect)

898
00:30:05,433 --> 00:30:06,890
- Terrible thing last night.

899
00:30:06,890 --> 00:30:08,903
We could hardly understand Betty at all.

900
00:30:08,903 --> 00:30:10,580
- [Crow] It's the chair sir.

901
00:30:10,580 --> 00:30:13,000
- Mr. Royson, I'd like
to talk to your daughter.

902
00:30:13,000 --> 00:30:14,200
- [Crow] Hey, take a number, pal.

903
00:30:14,200 --> 00:30:16,240
- She had a rough time last night.

904
00:30:16,240 --> 00:30:17,890
I don't think she's up yet.

905
00:30:17,890 --> 00:30:20,520
- Listen, she's lucky she can wake up.

906
00:30:20,520 --> 00:30:22,060
Would you get Betty, please?

907
00:30:22,060 --> 00:30:23,879
I'd like to ask her some questions.

908
00:30:23,879 --> 00:30:26,250
- Of course, Lieutenant,
I'll get her right away.

909
00:30:26,250 --> 00:30:28,430
- [Servo] God, I would trade
places with you, well, anyway.

910
00:30:28,430 --> 00:30:30,760
- Do you have any idea who
it might be, Lieutenant?

911
00:30:30,760 --> 00:30:31,920
How about some coffee?

912
00:30:31,920 --> 00:30:34,210
- No, thank you, I'll pass this time.

913
00:30:34,210 --> 00:30:35,710
From what you informed us last night,

914
00:30:35,710 --> 00:30:37,784
your daughter didn't get
a positive identification?

915
00:30:37,784 --> 00:30:38,980
- Well, that's what she said.

916
00:30:38,980 --> 00:30:40,470
- What time did you daughter
get home last night?

917
00:30:40,470 --> 00:30:42,420
- Well, I really don't know for sure.

918
00:30:42,420 --> 00:30:44,383
You see my wife and I
were out at the time.

919
00:30:44,383 --> 00:30:45,221
- I see.

920
00:30:45,221 --> 00:30:46,054
- [Crow] Enough said.

921
00:30:46,054 --> 00:30:47,060
- Yes, we were at the Fredrick.

922
00:30:47,060 --> 00:30:48,532
A business meeting, you know.

923
00:30:48,532 --> 00:30:49,365
- [Servo] Yeah.

924
00:30:49,365 --> 00:30:50,930
- Well, the first call came in around 2AM.

925
00:30:50,930 --> 00:30:51,870
Is that right?

926
00:30:51,870 --> 00:30:53,710
- Well, that's when we came home.

927
00:30:53,710 --> 00:30:55,750
I believe it was you
who called here later.

928
00:30:55,750 --> 00:30:57,393
- Yes, sir, that was around 3AM.

929
00:30:58,350 --> 00:31:00,130
- Quite a night between calls.

930
00:31:00,130 --> 00:31:01,620
- I had to stay home
the day for my business.

931
00:31:01,620 --> 00:31:02,650
- [Servo] I had diarrhea.

932
00:31:02,650 --> 00:31:03,790
- It's frightening to
think a thing like this

933
00:31:03,790 --> 00:31:05,210
could almost happen to your daughter.

934
00:31:05,210 --> 00:31:07,610
- It happened to someone's
daughter, Mr. Royson.

935
00:31:07,610 --> 00:31:09,290
Someone's daughter who was
out with your daughter,

936
00:31:09,290 --> 00:31:11,400
until all hours of the night.

937
00:31:11,400 --> 00:31:12,350
- Now, see here, Lieutenant.

938
00:31:12,350 --> 00:31:13,200
- [Crow] Stick it where the sun don't-

939
00:31:13,200 --> 00:31:15,750
- My daughter, she has to be in by 10PM.

940
00:31:15,750 --> 00:31:17,540
We can't watch over her
like an old mother hen.

941
00:31:17,540 --> 00:31:18,520
- [Servo] Bock, bock.

942
00:31:18,520 --> 00:31:19,637
- Why pick on my innocent little girl

943
00:31:19,637 --> 00:31:21,510
who was almost killed last night herself?

944
00:31:21,510 --> 00:31:23,730
- Nobody is picking on
your daughter, Mr. Royson.

945
00:31:23,730 --> 00:31:25,390
But you and every other
parent in town has known

946
00:31:25,390 --> 00:31:26,460
about these attacks

947
00:31:26,460 --> 00:31:29,070
and it's your responsibility
to watch out after your kids.

948
00:31:29,070 --> 00:31:30,810
- And your responsibility too.

949
00:31:30,810 --> 00:31:32,520
You're getting paid for it, Lieutenant.

950
00:31:32,520 --> 00:31:34,150
That's your job as a cop.

951
00:31:34,150 --> 00:31:35,183
- And what's your job as a parent?

952
00:31:35,183 --> 00:31:36,896
- [Servo] Are you as turned on as I am?

953
00:31:36,896 --> 00:31:39,896
(upbeat rock music)

954
00:31:44,920 --> 00:31:46,530
- Oh, I do hope you and the lieutenant

955
00:31:46,530 --> 00:31:47,860
are getting on real well.

956
00:31:47,860 --> 00:31:49,360
- [Crow] Shut up.

957
00:31:49,360 --> 00:31:51,520
- Betty will be down in
just a moment, Lieutenant.

958
00:31:51,520 --> 00:31:53,431
Can I get you a cup of
coffee or something?

959
00:31:53,431 --> 00:31:54,275
- No, thank you, ma'am.

960
00:31:54,275 --> 00:31:55,108
- [Mike] May I show you my slip?

961
00:31:55,108 --> 00:31:56,180
- Dear, did you tell the Michelsons

962
00:31:56,180 --> 00:31:58,130
we won't be over this evening?

963
00:31:58,130 --> 00:32:00,119
This has been quite a shock
to both of us, Lieutenant.

964
00:32:00,119 --> 00:32:03,047
We really do feel we should
stay home with Betty tonight.

965
00:32:03,047 --> 00:32:05,573
That is right isn't it, Lieutenant?

966
00:32:06,490 --> 00:32:07,900
- [Mike] Easy now, almost there.

967
00:32:07,900 --> 00:32:09,293
They're only stairs.

968
00:32:10,860 --> 00:32:12,767
Oh no, more stairs.

969
00:32:12,767 --> 00:32:14,840
- Sit down here.

970
00:32:14,840 --> 00:32:16,690
- [Crow] Pardon the stain, I'm a cop.

971
00:32:18,425 --> 00:32:19,940
(farting sound)

972
00:32:19,940 --> 00:32:21,110
- I'd like you to tell me everything

973
00:32:21,110 --> 00:32:22,630
you can about last night.

974
00:32:22,630 --> 00:32:24,560
- Yes, sir, I understand.

975
00:32:24,560 --> 00:32:25,925
- [Mike] I kissed my
boyfriend and the girl died.

976
00:32:25,925 --> 00:32:28,818
- It was so horrible.

977
00:32:28,818 --> 00:32:29,685
- There, there, dear

978
00:32:29,685 --> 00:32:31,720
- Pleas, Mrs. Royson, let me handle this.

979
00:32:31,720 --> 00:32:33,753
- Betty, I want you to
tell us everything you can.

980
00:32:33,753 --> 00:32:35,230
In the first place.

981
00:32:35,230 --> 00:32:36,490
Why did you come in so late?

982
00:32:36,490 --> 00:32:39,180
- [Crow] Are you now or have
you ever been a communist?

983
00:32:39,180 --> 00:32:40,640
- I was with Jimmy last night.

984
00:32:40,640 --> 00:32:41,800
- Jimmy?

985
00:32:41,800 --> 00:32:43,427
How many times have I told you

986
00:32:43,427 --> 00:32:44,730
I don't want you running
around with that wild kid.

987
00:32:44,730 --> 00:32:45,841
- Jimmy is not wild.

988
00:32:45,841 --> 00:32:47,610
- Mr. Royson, let me do the talking.

989
00:32:47,610 --> 00:32:48,710
- Yes, Lieutenant.

990
00:32:48,710 --> 00:32:49,543
- [Servo] Jag off.

991
00:32:49,543 --> 00:32:50,510
- [Crow] What was that?

992
00:32:51,740 --> 00:32:53,800
- Please Mrs. Royson, I'd
like to talk to Betty.

993
00:32:53,800 --> 00:32:55,210
- [Crow] Please clear the shot.

994
00:32:55,210 --> 00:32:57,932
- [Mike] Looks like mom has
won some dirt track trophies.

995
00:32:57,932 --> 00:32:58,765
(robots laugh)

996
00:32:58,765 --> 00:33:00,180
- Betty, where were you last night?

997
00:33:00,180 --> 00:33:01,780
- [Servo] I waited for you for hours.

998
00:33:01,780 --> 00:33:03,730
- Well, Jimmy and I drove around a bit.

999
00:33:04,690 --> 00:33:06,740
I planned to meet Anne at the school.

1000
00:33:06,740 --> 00:33:07,960
We were going to tell our folks

1001
00:33:07,960 --> 00:33:10,280
that we'd been working at the library.

1002
00:33:10,280 --> 00:33:11,113
- [Crow] This is hot, hot, hot.

1003
00:33:11,113 --> 00:33:15,040
- Anne, and I met at the
school about 12:30 - 1 o'clock.

1004
00:33:15,040 --> 00:33:17,000
- [Lieutenant] Betty, we're
dealing with a thrill killer.

1005
00:33:17,000 --> 00:33:17,833
A mad man.

1006
00:33:17,833 --> 00:33:19,670
If you can remember anything.

1007
00:33:19,670 --> 00:33:20,510
- [Mike] Punch it up a little.

1008
00:33:20,510 --> 00:33:21,780
Sell me this mad man.

1009
00:33:21,780 --> 00:33:22,936
- Lieutenant.

1010
00:33:22,936 --> 00:33:23,860
- [Lieutenant] Yes?

1011
00:33:23,860 --> 00:33:25,830
- [Servo] Yes, go on, more, more.

1012
00:33:25,830 --> 00:33:27,140
- It couldn't have been one of the kids.

1013
00:33:27,140 --> 00:33:28,971
- [Crow] They were all good Lutherans.

1014
00:33:28,971 --> 00:33:29,804
- Oh yeah.

1015
00:33:29,804 --> 00:33:31,410
- It couldn't have, could it?

